{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The small metric screw assortment fits my recent interest in bolts, nuts, and washers, and its M2 sizes add something beyond the M3–M5 kit I already chose.",
    "The digital caliper connects to measuring and matching fasteners, although I would wait for a project that requires precise measurements before buying it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The printer filaments require a printing need that I have never shown; buying hardware does not mean I own or use a 3D printer.",
    "The wire connectors and heat shrink tubing serve electrical wiring tasks, while my recent choices concern mechanical fasteners and magnetic hooks.",
    "The feeler gauge measures clearances, but I have no current task requiring that particular measurement."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in a few practical hardware supplies seems to have been extended to supplies for unrelated workshop projects.",
    "The screw kit described as being for electronics seems to have been taken as interest in wiring supplies, even though I chose mechanical fastening parts."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My two recent magnetic hook choices suggest an interest in attaching or hanging things on magnetic surfaces that these recommendations barely address.",
    "Useful additions to my existing fasteners, such as a missing screw size, matter more to me than another item broadly associated with making or repairing things.",
    "I rarely choose something without a concrete need, so even a potentially useful measuring tool is something I would defer until a project calls for it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in small fasteners but stretched it into printing and electrical projects that my recent choices do not support."
}"}
